# Compliance artifacts must be localized (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-08-16): **localize rules for products.**
The following compliance surfaces are **must-localize** — English-only
shipping text is a defect.

## The rule

> **Every compliance artifact this product shows, exports, or files must
> have localized catalogs for every Tier 1 content language. Preferred
> language on the person record wins when set; otherwise the page cookie
> / Accept-Language / English (US). Operators can edit each language’s
> version. Official regulation text stays in the language the authority
> published; AIC chrome, mappings, notices, and summaries are localized.**

## Must-localize list

| Artifact | Typical home |
| --- | --- |
| Audit reports | Report Center catalogs + export chrome |
| Evidence exports | Binder / auditor package export |
| Policy documentation | Playbooks, policy templates, docs |
| Risk assessment templates | Risks catalogs + SPA `risks` |
| Regulatory mappings (IEC 62443, NERC CIP, CMMC, ISO 27001) | Catalog + binder mapping chrome |
| Legal text (privacy, data handling, retention, chain-of-custody) | Disclosures + legal notices |
| Session recording evidence summaries | Recording / session evidence chrome |
| Access control evidence | IAM / access evidence reports |
| Change management logs | Change / CM evidence views |
| Incident response documentation | IR playbooks, notices, exports |
| Data processing agreements | Legal / DPA templates |
| Consent and privacy notices | Disclosures, welcome, training |
| Compliance dashboards | Dashboard / CSC / operations chrome |

A new row on this list lands with **every Tier 1** catalog key in the
same change set (or an honest **BLOCKED** with the missing tag named).

## Language tiers (compliance documentation)

These tags are for **filings, audit evidence, certification packages,
and legal text** — not optional chrome. BCP-47 folder names are the
catalog keys. Source identifiers stay US English
([`enterprise-compliance.mdc`](enterprise-compliance.mdc) §1).

**Shipped catalogs today:** `en`, `de`, `fr`, `es` (Wave A complete vs
current `en` key set). Tier 1 also requires `en-GB`, `zh-Hans`, and
`zh-TW` — treat as **BLOCKED** until those packs land and the installer
harvests them. Do not claim Tier 1 complete early.

**Pack plumbing:** `core-assets/content/language-packs/manifest.json`
(product tags, tier, `dir`, country, flag). Leaves use
`{ "text", "source_sha256" }` (hash of UTF-8 NFC of US English). Tools:
`scripts/language-packs/language_packs.py`. Developer standard:
`core-assets/docs/language-pack-developer-standard.md`. Picker shows
**flag + display name + BCP-47 tag** when two or more packs are installed;
hide the flag for a single-pack install. No CyberArk-style missing-key
English fallback.

